1521070.steps:
1. Activate the license of DNS Filtering;
2. Policy \ Rules and Policies \ DNS Rules, check the license icon;
3. Deregister the user, then check the DNS Filtering license icon.

1521071.steps:
1. Policy \ Rules and Policies \ DNS Rules, check the page;
2. Add some policies with different items(name/action/schedule/Zone/...);
3. Click every column( except PROFILE ), check the policies. Column PROFILE can not sort policies by design.

1521072.steps:
1. Policy \ Rules and Policies \ DNS Rules, add some enabled policies with different items (name/action/schedule/Zone¦);
2. Click search icon, enter any policy name, check the policies;
3. Disable one policy, select Inactive Rules from Active & Inactive drop-down box;
4. Select Active Rules;
5. Send traffic to match one policy, select Used Rules from Used & Unused drop-down box;
6. Select Unused Rules since last 60 seconds;
7. Wait for 2 minutes, click Refresh.

1521072.result:
In step 2, The policy with specified name is filtered correctly;

In step 3, the disabled policy displays;

In step 4, the enabled policies display;

In step 5, the matched policy displays;
In step 6, the non-matched policies display;
In step 7, the all policies display.

1521073.steps:
1. Policy \ Rules and Policies \ DNS Rules, add a policy named Test, Zone-LAN, Service-DNS Group, action-Proxy, Priority-manual 1, Enable;
2. PC connect to LAN interface X0, set the DNS of PC as X0 IP;
3. From PC, dig some domains;
4. In DNS Policy page, check Test Policy HITS.

1521074.steps:
1. Policy \ Rules and Policies \ DNS Rules, Click Add;
2. Check the Add DNS Policy window;
3. From CLI in config mode, enter 'dns-policy test'(test is a new name), 'commit', then 'show dns-policy test', check the action.

1521079.steps:
1. Policy \ Rules and Policies \ DNS Rules;
2. Add 32/64/128 valid policy entries;
3. Add one more policy.

1521079.result:
In step2, success;
In step3, error prompts.
The max count is not the same for different Platforms, refers to this page:<br />https://engineering.eng.sonicwall.com/pages/viewpage.action?pageId=153357828

1521085.steps:
1. Policy \ Rules and Policies \ DNS Rules, add a policy named TestEdit;
2. Select TestEdit policy, click Edit icon on the bottom of page;
3. Change some items(name/action/..), update;
4. Mouse hovers on the entry, the Edit icon shows, then click it, repeat step3.

1521088.steps:
1. Object \ Profile Object \ DNS Filtering, add some different profiles;
2. Policy \ Rules and Policies \ DNS Rules, click Add and select 'Filter' action;
3. Check the Profile drop-down box and select a custom profile;
4. Click Config icon of the box, change the profile items;
5. Click Config icon of the box, add a new profile.

1521088.result:
In step 3, the all profiles display and can be selected;

In step 4, the changes of the custom profile can be saved;

In step 5, the new profile can be added successfully and display in the box.

1521092.steps:
1. Policy \ Rules and Policies \ DNS Rules, click Add;
2. Check the Schedule drop-down box and select a schedule;
3. Click Config icon of the box, change the schedule items;
4. Click Config icon of the box, add a new schedule.

1521092.result:
In step 2, the all Schedules display and can be selected;

In step 3, the changes of the schedule can be saved;

In step 4, the new schedule can be added successfully and display in the box.

1521097.steps:
1. Policy \ Rules and Policies \ DNS Rules, click Add;
2. Check the Address drop-down box and select an address;
3. Click Config icon of the box, add a new address A;
4. Click Config icon of the box, add a new address group AG;
5. Click Config icon of the box, edit the A and AG.
(Default Address and Groups can not be edit)

1521097.result:
In step 2, the all IPv4 address and address groups display and can be selected;
**Refer to GEN7-44899, MAC Address or FQDN, and the address groups including them should be hidden in the drop down box**

In step 3-4, A and AG can be added successfully and display in the box;
**Refer to GEN7-44899, MAC Address or FQDN, should be hidden in the adding address/address-group page**

In step 5,  the changes of A and AG can be saved.

1521098.steps:
1. Object \ Match Objects \ Zones, add a custom zone named TestZ;
2. Policy \ Rules and Policies \ DNS Rules, click Add;
3. Edit and select a New Schedule named TestS;
4. Edit and select a New Address named TestA, and select Zone as TestZ, click Add;
5. Match Objects \ Zones page, try to delete TestZ;
6.  Match Objects \ Addresses page, try to delete TestA.
7.  Match Objects \ Schedules page, try to delete TestS.

1521098.result:
In step 4, the policy added successfully;

In step 5, error prompts : This zone object is in used by a DNS policy;

In step 6, error prompts : This address object is in used by a DNS policy;

In step 7, error prompts : This Schedule object is in used by a DNS policy.

1521101.steps:
1. Policy \ Rules and Policies \ DNS Rules, click Add;
2. To Optional Settings, edit a valid number in the textbox og Number of Connections allowed;
3. Check the Enable Connection Threshold for each Source IP, enter a valid number, click Save.

1521102.steps:
1. Policy \ Rules and Policies \ DNS Rules, click Add Top;
2. Enable Show Diagram;
3. Change the configuration on the Add Page, check the Diagram.

1521105.steps:
1. Policy \ Rules and Policies \ DNS Rules, Add some policies;
2. Select one policy, click Move Up on the bottom;
3. Select one policy, click Move Down on the bottom;
4. Mouse hovers on the left Drag icon of one policy, then drag the policy up and down.

1521105.result:
In step 2, the policy moves up;
In step 3, the policy moves down;
In step 4, the policy can moves with mouse.

1521106.steps:
1. Policy \ Rules and Policies \ DNS Rules, Add some policies;
2. Click Live Counters on the bottom;
3. Send traffic through the policies;
4. Click Pause Counters on the bottom;
5. Click Clear Counters on the bottom.

1521106.result:
In step 2, the Hit number changes to Green and update with the traffic, and the Live Counters changes to Pause Counters;

In step 4, the Hit number changes to Default black and keep stable without Refresh, and the Pause Counters changes to Live Counters;

In step 5, All Hit numbers change to 0.

1521107.steps:
1. Policy \ Rules and Policies \ DNS Rules, Add a policy named TestClone;
2. Select the TestClone, click Clone Up on the bottom;
3. Select the TestClone_clone, click Clone Down on the bottom.

1521130.steps:
1. Object \ Profile Objects \ DNS Filtering ;
2. Add a valid profile;
3. Edit the existing profile, change the name and actions.
